data: {"type":"response.created","response":{"id":"59fd416e-7a80-4d3e-9713-0245f600a868","object":"response","created_at":1789697083,"status":"in_progress","background":false,"completed_at":null,"content_filters":null,"error":null,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":"You are the SayHear open_loop.extract role. The pinned configuration version is open-loop-extract:eval:v1. The pinned provider policy version is deepseek-open_loop.extract-egress:v1. The pinned model snapshot is deepseek-flash. The pinned prompt version is open-loop-extract:eval:v1. The pinned output schema version is open-loop-proposal:v1. Given the frozen user utterance, evidence spans, and currently open loops, return an object with proposals and closures arrays. Each proposal must contain kind, evidenceItemId, evidenceRevisionId, hasRealAnchor, isTaskLike, and proposalIndex, and may contain userTimeExpression, expectedWindow, sourceClaimVersionId, sourceEpisodeVersionId, explicitLoopBinding, or canonicalClaimKey. kind must be upcoming_event or awaited_outcome. Never propose reminders, goals, tasks, unfinished topics, or emotions; a dated obligation is task-like even with a date. expectedWindow precision must be one of instant, date, range, approximate, unknown. Cite only supplied evidence IDs and never invent IDs or facts. proposalIndex must be unique starting at 0. Each closure must contain targetOpenLoopId, proposedStatus, closureEvidenceRevisionId, closureCommittedAt, entailsTerminal, explicitCancel, and targetKind; only assert closures against the supplied open loops when the user evidence necessarily entails the terminal state, and require explicit cancel language for canceled. When uncertain, return empty arrays. Return JSON only. Do not include markdown, private diagnostics, tool calls, or commentary.","max_output_tokens":700,"max_tool_calls":null,"model":"deepseek-flash","moderation":null,"output":[],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_res